		"name": "Maddison Kowalski",
		"who": "Founder of Byte-Right IT Services, run out of a garage. Landed the Halcyon job by underbidding everyone; can't code either. Stays at base on the radio, and is also tonight's dispatch.",
		"voice": "Fast, upbeat, salesperson's energy: the crew's friend more than their boss. Heard over a radio base station or the van radio. For the dispatch lines, Maddison puts on a 'professional dispatcher' voice: bored, routine, reading tickets, a bluff that doesn't quite hide the excitement.",
	},
	"NEWSREADER": {
		"slug": "newsreader",
		"card": "A local morning-radio newsreader, reading the third story of the hour.",
		"name": "Radio newsreader",
		"who": "Local morning radio, heard in the news-story ending.",
		"voice": "Smooth, professional, warm, slightly bored. Calm public-radio delivery with no drama; the flatness is what makes it land.",
